# Preserve a declaration's source role on its existing operation. Its operands,
# physical destination and execution opcode do not change. Replace only that
# operation's typed code record, in the operation's arena and physical profile;
# materialized value cells gain no wrapper.
# Value, typed-role classification and throws-boundary operations are maintained
# by the generated L2 lmx_walk_values module above. Explicit contexts stay here.

# N4 THE DATA PLACES OF A SPLIT CALL (lmx_walk.h, PLACE and CALL_DATA).  The two CHAR_PTR cells at `at` and
# `at + 1` of a PLACE or CALL_DATA frame: the module's layout tokens and the procedure's static place table.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# At the activation's entry (lmx_walk_entry_node), before any body statement and outside every nested call's scratch
# mark: the row of the PLACE's table for this activation's data, its slots taken from the activation's scratch.  One
# table per activation.  A second table, a row that is not YES -- the call's admission refuses such data first, with
# the implicit `call` -- or a table with no names is the translator's broken promise: INVALID (X1).
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# The data slot of name r of a PLACE: the row its activation resolved at entry.  A PLACE of another table, or one
# the entry did not resolve, or r past the row: INVALID (X1).  Nothing is resolved here.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# 1 when p is the Structure root or a Structure whose parent chain reaches it.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# The slot a node names by its two operands at `first`: the Structure that holds the
# field, by reference, and the number of the slot inside it.  k.4 (no cached plan, no
# membership set -- next_core_tasks.md §3 item 9): the holder must classify as a Structure
# and the index must be within its own `array.size`, asked here, every time, unconditionally --
# there is no separate counting/prepare pass left to have asked it once.  A translator
# mistake that names an arbitrary operator node or literal fails this same check.
# A compact OWN/AT operand is itself a Structure whose child1 stores the output;
# both implicit and explicit coordinates resolve that same physical place.
# `write` refuses a holder in the exact qualified
# immutable profile (lmx_walk_immutable); a read (`write = 0`) never does.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# Replay only the accessed owned edge chain in the existing unequal-occurrence
# ABI. Foreign/ancestor holders stay themselves. A missing corresponding edge
# is not permission to write the original occurrence. This creates no graph
# or mapping registry; ordinary execution already has code == node.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# A zero holder names the selected occurrence. Fixed holders inside the
# original executing body follow its actual child edges in the selected
# occurrence; evaluated OF/OWN_OF references do not use this projection.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: the slot an own-field node names, with its holder and index.  OWN [own, holder, slot] names its holder by
# reference, under lmx_walk_slot's rules (a Structure, never an op node; `write` refuses the exact immutable
# profile).  OWN_OF [own_of, holder-expr, slot] and SET_OF [set_of, holder-expr, slot, value] evaluate theirs -- a
# nested body's Structure -- under the same rules.  Any other node is INVALID.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: the working table's row of `slot`, or 0.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: one row of the working table, loaded now from `slot` (holder's child `index`) and clean, linked after the last
# row; a slot that already has one keeps it.  A number is kind 1 (its value and type), a pointer cell kind 2 (the
# reference it holds), a Structure slot kind 3 (the Structure, or 0 while empty).  The row is taken from the scratch
# store after the activation's mark and is gone with its rewind.
# THE PROMISED CELL (2026-10-14): OWN/OWN_OF of a reference binding are four wide, SET_OF is five wide; the
# last child carries the typed cell its construction promised at the slot -- the translator's witness
# (l2_rw_ownnode/l2_rw_write), a pointer cell, as ARG
# carries its type witness at child 3.  Such a slot must hold a pointer cell of the witness's exact storage type
# (lmx_walk_pointer_cells_alike: one pool type, stride and accessors; an imported sealed cell of that type seen
# through the range index is as good as a local one) -- the test the native entry load makes with its static type
# (lmx_pointer_value_promised, lmx_value_owned.lm1) -- so the row is kind 2 and the nothing it holds is the valid
# nothing, the implicit `interpreter` throw at the reader.  The slot emptied, holding something that is not a pointer
# cell, or holding a pointer cell of another type, is the construction's broken promise: INVALID (X1) here, before
# any read -- never a kind-3 row that reads as an empty Structure slot, takes the binding's SET and publishes its
# value into the slot as a Structure reference (lmx_walk_publish, kind 3), and never a type read off whatever the
# slot holds.  A witness with a noncanonical ABI, or a widened node whose witness is absent, is damaged: INVALID.
# A four-wide OWN whose child 3 is not a pointer cell is itself damaged: INVALID, not a node without a
# witness.  Measured 2026-10-14 before the witness: the driver's null-path and swap-root-fields mutants of
# unit_at_pointer_cell_catch walked to exit 7; before the exact type, the erased witness child of that program and
# the swap of two present cells of different pointer types (unit_at_pointer_cell_typed) walked to exit 7.  A node
# without the witness -- a number's or a direct Structure slot's OWN, OWN_OF, SET_OF -- is classified by the slot's
# content, as before.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: whether `holder` belongs to this activation -- its data, its code, or a body lexically inside them (up the
# parent links).  Another occurrence's Structure does not: an own node naming it gets no row.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: THE ENTRY LOAD (Lingvamyxa spec 21.5). The same executable-body
# traversal that snapshots hidden inputs visits the OWN applications whose
# values this activation uses. A nested callable declaration is not executed
# by its enclosing activation and supplies no working row here.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: a copied occurrence has copied applications and lexical parents; bare
# role records remain shared. Field cells are not entered by the body traversal.
# Passive body observation and load_body are maintained in L2 values.
# The ordinary build recipe selects a foreign constant0/1 before C compilation;
# no late ifdef, stub observer, new callback context or ABI is introduced.

# One executable-body traversal serves both entry preparations: mode 0 collects
# consumed hidden inputs, mode 1 loads own fields. A body executes only OP
# fields; a nested callable definition is a plain Structure, not its step.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.


# Within an OP, visit its physically owned expression OPs and its explicitly
# executable body operands. Other plain Structure operands are data or other
# callables; scanning their bodies would borrow another activation's inputs.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# §7b: THE PUBLICATION (book §12, §14; Lingvamyxa spec 21.6) -- every dirty row, in row order (the order the entry
# load made them), written into its slot: a number by its cell's type, a pointer into its pointer cell, a Structure as
# the slot's reference; then unmarked.  A clean row is never written.  A failed store is INVALID (X1); the rows after
# it stay dirty.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# SET_ARG changes only this activation's input value; caller storage and lexical
# fallback cells remain unchanged. All input places are activation-owned and stable.
# Allocate input places at activation entry, outside every nested-call scratch
# mark. Their values may be loaded lazily from the per-ARG declared witness.


# The per-input address remains stable through calls, rebinding and address-of.

# Load after resolution, preserving the explicit cell owner's context even
# when the destination aliases that owner. No address-to-Model lookup occurs.



# A recoverable fault of a valid operation -- a zero divisor, an index past the
# descriptor, a null reference or Array -- is the ordinary implicit throw
# `interpreter`: no payload, and no landing chosen here.  The bodies above find
# the pad by lexical parentage (lmx_walk_body).  Nothing on the node says this.

# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# One physical-place resolution for reads, explicit stores and ADDRESS.
# ELEM selects backing storage here, before any char value or pointer is loaded.

# Item 4 of the interpreter-throw closure (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md): THE MINIMAL WIDTH OF AN EXECUTED
# OPERATION -- its role cell and the children it reads unconditionally -- checked before any operand of it is
# evaluated (lmx_walk_eval, lmx_walk_place), so a malformed frame never runs part of itself and its refusal never
# depends on an operand's value: INVALID, a graph-invariant diagnostic, not a throw.  Read from the operations
# themselves: RET [ret (value)]; CALL [call callee ...] (its long form checks its own five); EXEC five; LIT two; OWN
# two (the one-cell form) and OWN_OF three; AT two (the one-cell form), OF/DEREF/ELEM three; ARG four (index, fallback,
# witness); SET_ARG four; PUT three, PUT_OF/ELEMPUT/PUT_REF four; SET three, SET_OF four; the two-operand operators
# three; NEG/POS two (exact, their own check); IF three (the else arm is a fourth); WHILE/UNTIL three, FOR four;
# AND/OR three; ADDRESS three; GUARD three (exact, its own check); GUARDED, SELF, NODE, EMPTY, BREAK, CONTINUE one;
# PRIM/PRIM_PUB three (their own check); THROW three (its own check); LENGTH two; NAMED three.  A PAD is one: a pad
# without a key takes nothing but is no operand; ADMIT_AS and EXPECT_INT read their own shapes; retained source frames
# are inert.  Fixed-width operations keep their exact checks after this minimum.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# QUALIFIED IMMUTABILITY at the point of every write (k.4: OWN/SET target via lmx_walk_slot, PUT_REF/PUT_OF at
# their own sites, PRIM through its owner) -- there is no separate prepare pass any more.  Read first from the range
# index (RR2b, steps/qualifier-receivers-20261010.md): a cell whose array carries a sealed nonzero profile belongs to a
# qualified branch, static or made at run time (lmx_range_sealed_profile), whatever lists the frame's context carries
# -- a value qualified at run time is in no list.  Then the exact profile the context names and the program's qualified
# roots, as before.  Ownership is irrelevant, and so is the sealing of an UNPROFILED array (the MSG pool sealed for
# import): a foreign or sealed address of another profile is not made immutable by accident.
# Body moved to the ordinary machine module lmx_walk_values.lm2.

# ---- execution -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The external callable ABI carries declared-width value storage for arguments.
# A typed evaluation result is converted once here: scalar into the supplied
# destination, held reference through out, and absent/void through out = 0.
fn: lmx_walk_call_prim_dispatch (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; @: Lmx data; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out; @: LmxWalkValue lmx_input_values; @: LmxWalkValue lmx_result_context) int
    LmxArena: sa
    LmxPool: cells
    LmxScratch: scratch
    LmxWalkContext: ctx
    LmxWalkValue: result
    int: st
    int: rty 0
    size_t: wv 0U
    if: out = 0
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    \out: 0
    if: arena = 0 || code = 0 || data = 0
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    memset((cast: (@: void) (@ sa)), 0, c.sizeof(c.LmxArena))
    memset((cast: (@: void) (@ cells)), 0, c.sizeof(c.LmxPool))
    memset((cast: (@: void) (@ scratch)), 0, c.sizeof(c.LmxScratch))
    memset((cast: (@: void) (@ ctx)), 0, c.sizeof(c.LmxWalkContext))
    if: lmx_arena_open(@ sa) != 0
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    if: lmx_scratch_open(@ scratch, @ sa, @ cells, 64U) != c.LMX_SCRATCH_OK
        lmx_arena_release(@ sa)
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    ---
    ctx.arena: arena
    ctx.scratch: @ scratch
    ctx.immutable_roots: lmx_walk_program_roots_g
    ctx.immutable_root_count: lmx_walk_program_root_count_g
    # The call site has already selected its data. Pointer identity does not
    # distinguish a unary call from explicit `call: code code`.
    st: lmx_walk_activate_values(@ ctx, code, data, refs, nargs, lmx_input_values, @ result)
    lmx_scratch_close(@ scratch)
    lmx_arena_release(@ sa)
    if: st = c.LMX_WALK_STOPPED
        return: 0
    if: st != c.LMX_WALK_OK
        # Errors abort; a throw is returned as the selected callee's ordinal.
        if: st >= c.LMX_WALK_THROWN
            \out: result.ref
            st: lmx_walk_boundary_status(arena, 0, code, st)
        ---
        return: lmx_call_note_walk_fail(st)
    ---
    if: result.present = 0
        return: 0
    if: result.kind = c.LMX_WALK_VALUE_REFERENCE
        if: lmx_result_context != 0
            lmx_value_context_copy(lmx_result_context, @ result)
        \out: result.ref
        return: 0
    # A statement-position call may discard a numeric body-last value. The
    # typed value is already detached from activation scratch; no int box is
    # fabricated for a caller that supplied no result destination.
    if: dest = 0
        return: 0
    if: lmx_walk_value_number(@ result, @ wv, @ rty) != c.LMX_WALK_OK
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    if: lmx_walk_store_numeric_raw(dest, rty, wv) != c.LMX_WALK_OK
        return: c.LMX_CALL_NOT_CALLABLE
    \out: dest
return: 0
